---
description: Vibe-coding project rules — source of truth is AGENTS.md
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md first. It is the source of truth for stable project rules and commands; current progress lives in MEMORY.md and details in `agent_docs/`.
- For new work, propose a short plan; once it is approved, continue through implementation and checks in that scope without asking again for each edit.
- Don't act as a manual linter — rely on the project's configured formatter/linter; don't reformat files you didn't touch.
- Follow the authorization rules in AGENTS.md: confirm before deleting user data, applying a migration to a live database, deploying, or sending anything externally.
